comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-12T21:08:37.896Z","harness:codex","GitHub report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1244. Canonical tracking reused after complete all-status duplicate check."
  "2026-09-15T09:10:53.356Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance uncovered a real distinction: minimal governance permits quick capture but core metadata validation still warns about missing estimates and acceptance criteria. The documented scratch profile now explicitly selects custom required fields author and close_reason; close records resolution and expected/actual evidence. The real CLI regression verifies that this configured lifecycle passes complete validation without warnings. Only actively edited items remain in progress."
  "2026-09-15T09:19:01.204Z","harness:codex",First-run refusal regression initially failed at 20 lines. Missing and uninitialized tracker displays now pass the three-line contract while preserving tokenized exact-root recovery in JSON. Packed npm/npx/bunx smoke passed for six package fixtures. Focused lifecycle validation passes without warnings under the documented custom metadata profile.
  "2026-09-15T09:19:56.284Z","harness:codex","Manual fresh-directory acceptance passed using actual Node CLI subprocesses: init 11 lines, configured scratch lifecycle including both config commands 813 estimated tokens, 5.83 seconds, three created tasks, next selection, structured closure, and full validation ok with has_warnings=false. Sentry/telemetry threshold gate passed with critical=0 and high=0 across its 14-day window. This does not substitute for fresh post-merge telemetry correlation."
  "2026-09-15T09:27:39.439Z","harness:codex","Manual missing-tracker recovery passed in a temporary path containing spaces: next exited 3 with exactly three stderr lines; parsing and executing its emitted retry exited 0 and initialized the exact requested tracker root. Latest named SDK display type is exported from the public root, and TypeScript plus focused lint and docs links pass."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-15T09:25:32.535Z","harness:codex","Delivery scope combines scratch initialization, compact exact-root recovery, documented configurable metadata governance, and lifecycle/context acceptance. Existing SDK summary calls and full JSON InitResult remain compatible; the compact display has its own named public type. Broader roadmap and historical graph migrations retain their canonical open owners."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-15T09:24:17.315Z","harness:codex",Minimal capture governance and metadata validation are separate policies. A scratch recipe must configure both intentionally and verify full validation after closure; successful create/close exits alone do not prove a warning-free lifecycle.
